#codex-reply no, TinyFrame explicitly adds TF_SOF_BYTE to the checksum - https://github.com/MightyPork/TinyFrame/blob/a29167a69f052975b0e0134a73b4d31d03afa8fa/TinyFrame.c#L570

```
static void _TF_FN pars_begin_frame(TinyFrame *tf) {
    // Reset state vars
    CKSUM_RESET(tf->cksum);
#if TF_USE_SOF_BYTE
    CKSUM_ADD(tf->cksum, TF_SOF_BYTE);
#endif

    tf->discard_data = false;

    // Enter ID state
    tf->state = TFState_ID;
    tf->rxi = 0;
}
```
This suggests SOF byte is part of the checksum calculation
